  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nWave property of electrons implies that they will show diffraction effects. Davisson and Germer demonstrated this by diffracting electrons from crystals. The law governing the diffraction from a crystal is obtained by requiring that electron waves reflected from the planes of atoms in a crystal interfere constructively (see in figure).<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/tDXzo6k7R_tTpNA_mOrnSC8XPn3B0l4WIu-P1D-E49U.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nIf a strong diffraction peak is observed when electrons are incident at an angle 'i' from the normal to the crystal planes with distance ' $d$ ' between them (see figure), de Broglie wavelength $\\lambda_{\\mathrm{dB}}$ of electrons can be calculated by the relationship ( $n$ is an integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CKFcA",
      "text": "\n$d \\sin i=n \\lambda_{d B}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Jz96m",
      "text": "\n$2 d \\cos i=n \\lambda_{d B}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9FTBZ",
      "text": "\n$2 d \\sin i=n \\lambda_{d B}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qKf7o",
      "text": "\n$d \\cos i=n \\lambda_{d B}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
